1. What is encapsulation?
Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data (variables) and the methods that operate on that data into a single unit (class), while restricting direct access to the data.

In Java, we commonly achieve encapsulation by:
 Declaring class variables as private.
 Providing public getter and setter methods when access is required.
 Adding validation inside setter methods to control which values can be assigned.

 Hiding the sensitive detail while allowing controlled access